{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgShgDPpNft3YtbUUivUT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Friday in St. Louis: Grown-Folks Edition\n\n**Quick note:** This Friday is Oct 30, the night before Halloween, so expect costume parties and fuller rooms. I can't see live listings, so confirm hours and showtimes before you head out.\n\n### Midday: Rib Tips, Round One\n**Smoki O's** (North Broadway). It's Black-owned, a North City institution, and known for rib tips and snoots. While you're here, try the **snoot**, a crispy smoked pig snout that's a St. Louis specialty you won't find in most cities. They keep short hours, so go at lunch.\n\n### Afternoon: The Comedy Roots Tour\n- **The Ville / Greater Ville.** Drive past **Sumner High**, the first Black high school west of the Mississippi. Dick Gregory went there, along with Chuck Berry, Tina Turner, and Arthur Ashe.\n- **The Griot Museum of Black History.** It's small and personal, a good stop if it's open (hours are limited).\n- **Fun fact for your crew:** Redd Foxx was born in St. Louis, and Cedric the Entertainer grew up in nearby Berkeley. You're in Kings of Comedy country.\n\n### Early Evening: Rib Tips, Round Two\n**C&K Barbecue** (Jennings Station Rd) or **Roper's Ribs** (Natural Bridge). Both are neighborhood spots with no tourist energy. Get tips with sauce on top of the fries. Bring cash just in case.\n\n### Night: Stand-Up\nCheck **Helium** (Brentwood) and **Funny Bone** (Westport) for who's headlining Friday. Also search Eventbrite and Instagram for local Black comedy showcases, which are often better than the club bookings.\n\n### Late: Before I Let Go\nFor Maze energy, you want a **grown & sexy R&B night or a steppers set**. Check:\n- **The Ambassador** (Dellwood), which hosts R&B and old-school shows\n- **Majic 104.9** and **Hot 104.1** event listings\n- Search \"steppers St. Louis Friday\"\n\nIf the DJ doesn't play \"Before I Let Go\" by midnight, you're in the wrong room.\n\nWant me to tighten this into a timed itinerary or adjust for a date or a group?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":647,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4dd89464-f645-4d5a-87e9-73dc1e127e67","uuid":"4b95a3b4-fd9d-4a6d-a29c-f961fbad77ae","timestamp":"2026-10-27T11:58:41.313Z","request_id":"req_011CgShgDARpGeQJmgovh6Uq"}
